blocks.en:
Minimal pairs, items differing in exactly one controlled dimension, are a standard diagnostic methodology in NLP.
The most notable examples include BLiMP ( Warstadt et al., 2020 ) and MultiBLiMP ( Jumelet et al., 2025 ) , which are sentence pairs isolating specific contrasts in syntax, morphology, and semantics. HANS ( McCoy et al., 2019 ) probes whether natural language inference models exploit syntactic heuristics rather than genuine reasoning;
WinoBias ( Zhao et al., 2018 ) with Winograd-style coreference pairs measures gender bias in NLP systems.

blocks.zh:
最小对子,在完全一个可控维度上不同的物品,是NLP中的一种标准诊断方法.
最显著的例子有: BLIMP(Warstadt等,2020年)和MultiBLIMP(Jumelet等,2025年),它们是句子对语法,形态学,语义学中的具体对比进行隔离. HANS(McCoy等,2019年)探究自然语言推论模型是否利用了合成heuristics而不是真正的推理;
WinoBias (Zhao等,2018年) 有Winograd风格的coference配对测量NLP系统中的性别偏见.
